verRestoreLaunchesWithNewestClosure` (launch under the fix; parked before it), `TestDecideSuccessorNullFoldParks`, `TestRunSuccessorNullFoldParks`, `TestRunPostTakeoverStaleBaseParks` | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-successor-nullfold.log` |\n19|| P1-1 profile closure from the handoff base | `Run` loads the closure from the checkpoint actually resumed — required checkpoint, else the fold's newest via `LoadCheckpoint`, else the session head — never `Winner.Checkpoint` (`run.go`); the unknown-store guard now keys on the published newest | `TestRunPostTakeoverLaunchCarriesNewestClosureStandardToYolo`, `TestRunPostTakeoverLaunchCarriesNewestClosureYoloToStandard` (both directions through `Run`), `TestRunNoCkptStorePublishedNewestFails`, `TestRunNewestAbsentFromStoreFails` | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-closure-source.log` (mutant re-reads `Winner.Checkpoint`, launches stale yolo, dies) |\n20|| P2-1 post-window same-pair race reports launch | `Store.Supersede`/`installPair` report the replay (`binding.go`, `(Binding, bool, error)`); `Run` flips the replayed post-window outcome to `ActionReattach` with the recorded receipt (`run.go`) | `TestRunPostWindowSamePairRaceReattaches` (hook-played race through `Run`); store-level `TestSupersedeConcurrentSamePairReplays` asserts the signal | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-supersede-replay.log` |\n21|| P3-1 window closes on the lease checkpoint | No production change (the predicate already reads the fold only); added the negative and the harness row | `TestRunWindowLeaseCheckpointNullFoldRefuses` | `mutants/pass1/N-window-lease-checkpoint.log` |\n22|| P3-2 `Run` swallows the fold error | No production change (the error already propagates); added the negative and the harness row | `TestRunUnfoldableChainFails` | `mutants/pass1/N-run-fold-error.log` |\n23|| P3-3 ratio 39/43 | Re-derived on the fixed tree (see below) | — (measurement, not a gate) | `ratio-check.log` |\n24|| P3-4 fabricated 27-command list | This document reports the configured `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` verbatim with real exits (see below) | — | `cmd/cmd01-*.log` … `cmd/cmd27-*.log` |\n25|| P3-5 phantom matrix names | rev4 matrix names only tests verified present via `go test -list` | — | `ratio-check.log` |\n26|| P3-6 `realmRowUsable` restates reconcile | Stated as a bound (code comment + TRACEABILITY): the aggregate `Reconcile` error carries no per-object identity and liveness shares the generic mismatch code, so no per-row verdict can be derived; classification-only, fail-closed both directions | `TestDecideExpiredRealmRowRefusesUnavailable`, `TestDecidePreRebootRealmRowRefusesUnavailable`, `TestDecideLiveRealmRowBackendFaultStands` (unchanged) | `axpane-test-v.log` |\n27|| P3-7 identity not bound to SESSION_ID | `checkProviderIdentity` binds the validated record's own `session_id` (`checkIdentitySession`, `decide.go`); foreign record refuses `invalid_config` | `TestDecideIdentityForeignSessionRefuses` | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-identity-session.log` |\n28|| P3-8 false prose | README profile sentence, TRACEABILITY rows, and the rev3 LOGBOOK entry (explicit REVERSAL paragraph, following the rev2 precedent) corrected | — | candidate diff |\n29|\n30|Stated bound added with P1-1: binding the handoff base to a\n31|checkpoint the chain published is the takeover leaf's obligation —\n32|this leaf compares the base against nothing (TRACEABILITY.md,\n33|`Decide` comment).\n34|\n35|## AC coverage: 43 of 43 rows driven\n36|\n37|Measured, not restated: 43 data rows counted in\n38|`internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`, every named test verified\n39|present via `go test -list`, zero rows without a named test, and\n40|the full package suite green (`ratio-check.log`,\n41|`axpane-test-v.log`: 192 `--- PASS`, 0 `--- FAIL`). The four rows\n42|the rev3 reviewer measured unfaithful now pin the post-takeover\n43|launch positives: materialization and checkpoint rows drive the\n44|C1-sourced launch and the stale-base park, the after-restore row\n45|drives both owners, and the profile row drives both directions\n46|plus the restore closure through `Run`.\n47|\n48|## Negative and mutant evidence\n49|\n50|- 11 new committed tests in `internal/axpane/rev4_test.go`, 3\n51|  rewritten in `rev3_test.go` (agreement negatives became the\n52|  diverged-base positive and the null-fold negative; the no-store\n53|  guard test follows the newest), plus replay-signal assertions\n54|  on the `Supersede` tests.\n55|- `mutant_harness.py`: 53/53 rows match on two full passes — 52\n56|  KILLED + the SURVIVED control. New rows: `N-successor-nullfold`\n57|  (null-fold conditional), `N-closure-source` (re-reads\n58|  `Winner.Checkpoint`), `N-supersede-replay` (replay keeps\n59|  launch), `N-window-lease-checkpoint`, `N-run-fold-error`,\n60|  `N-identity-session`, `N-run-newest-absent`; re-anchored:\n61|  `N-run-ckpt-store`, `N-supersede-no-replace`; deleted with the\n62|  equality: `N-materialization-agreement`, `N-checkpoint-agreement`.\n63|  Per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in `mutants/pass1/`\n64|  (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); production\n65|  blobs verified byte-identical before/after (`blob-oids-*.txt`).\n66|- Crash/idempotency: unchanged no-replace link commits on both\n67|  install paths, hook-armed seams, real-SIGKILL test; the replay\n68|  signal adds no new durable write.\n69|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate\n70|  inspects source text.\n71|\n72|## Validation suite (configured commands, in order)\n73|\n74|Every command below is quoted verbatim from\n75|`task-board.config.json`\n76|`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (27 commands) and\n77|was executed once against the exact candidate tree; logs in `cmd/`.\n78|\n79|| # | Command | Exit |\n80|| --- | --- | --- |\n81|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\"` | 0 |\n82|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n83|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n84|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 (38 packages ok, 21766 `--- PASS`, 0 package `FAIL`) |\n85|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | 0 (38 ok, 0 data races; axpane 17.5s) |\n86|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 (axpane 80.9%) |\n87|| 7–12 | rpcwire/scalar/canonicaljson fuzz ×6 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×6 |\n88|| 13–20 | secconftest fuzz ×8 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×8 |\n89|| 21 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (registry untouched: contracts=64, sections=36, clauses 49/569) |\n90|| 22 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0 |\n91|| 23 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n92|| 24 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n93|| 25 | JSON validation over tracked `*.json` | 0 |\n94|| 26 | `task-board validate` | 0 (185 pre-existing board-hygiene notes on other elements, unrelated to this candidate) |\n95|| 27 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n96|\n97|Note on cmd4: the log contains indented `--- FAIL` lines that are\n98|nested expected-failure output inside passing tests (e.g. the\n99|resumesmoke negative demonstrations); every package reports `ok`\n100|and the command exits 0.\n101|\n102|## Files changed\n103|\n104|- `internal/axpane/` (new package, still untracked):\n105|  `decide.go` (null-fold arm, agreement deleted, identity session\n106|  bind), `run.go` (closure source, newest-based guard,\n107|  replay flip), `binding.go` (replay signal), `errors.go`\n108|  (null-fold + identity causes), `doc.go`, `rev4_test.go` (new),\n109|  `rev3_test.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `mutant_harness.py`,\n110|  `TRACEABILITY.md` (rewrites above).\n111|- `README.md`: package section (additive: implication, closure\n112|  source, identity bind, 52-mutant count).\n113|- `LOGBOOK.md`: rev4 entry + explicit rev3 REVERSAL (additive).\n114|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n115|\n116|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n117|\n118|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added;\n119|mesh refresh is the caller-reported `Verified` fact; the\n120|dead-realm mapping fires only when the caller needs the realm\n121|row, submitted a realm row, and none is usable; the handoff-base\n122|binding is the takeover leaf's obligation; the realm usability\n123|predicate copy is classification-only. `internal/traceability`\n124|untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n125|\n126|## Handoff\n127|\n128|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n129|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n130|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_results-rev4.md`,\n131|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix-rev4.md`,\n132|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_rev4-evidence.tar.gz`.","final_result":true}}}
