{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c931","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b201-5e84-7ea0-8bc6-d79919cbe007"},"sequence":755,"recorded_at":1780531400001505,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9e30868d-563f-43f3-9fe7-d9ddb65377f0","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"9e30868d-563f-43f3-9fe7-d9ddb65377f0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9e30868d-563f-43f3-9fe7-d9ddb65377f0"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b203-c497-76c0-ba7f-777f5268bc7d"},"task_id":"01a0b203-c497-76c0-ba7f-777f5268bc7d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b203-c497-76c0-ba7f-777f5268bc7d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-26-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"terminal-instance-binding\\\" internal/ --include=*.go | grep -v _test | head -n 15; echo \\\"====\\\"; grep -rln \\\"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\\\" internal/ | head; echo \\\"====\\\"; sed -n '11440,11480p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Find binding schema owners and CLI Result 4\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go:82:\\t\\t\\t{Name: \\\"Terminal Instance binding\\\", ID: \\\"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\\\", Versions: []string{\\\"1.0.0\\\"}},\\ninternal/catalog/catalog_gen.go:144:\\t\\t\\t{Name: \\\"Terminal Instance binding\\\", ID: \\\"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\\\", Versions: []string{\\\"1.0.0\\\"}},\\ninternal/catalog/catalog_gen.go:209:\\t\\t\\t{Name: \\\"Terminal Instance binding\\\", ID: \\\"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\\\", Versions: []string{\\\"1.0.0\\\"}},\\ninternal/catalog/catalog_gen.go:296:\\t\\t{Definition: SelfIdentityContract{ContractID: \\\"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\\\", ContractVersions: []string{\\\"1.0.0\\\"}, SelfField: \\\"binding_id\\\", DiscriminatorName: \\\"\\\", DiscriminatorValue: \\\"\\\", NormativeSection: \\\"4.B\\\"}, Releases: []Release{Release(\\\"v0.5.0\\\"), Release(\\\"v0.6.0\\\"), Release(\\\"v0.7.0\\\")}},\\ninternal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go:137:\\tregister(\\\"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\\\", rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape, \\\"1.0.0\\\")\\n====\\ninternal/specpin/v0.7.0.lock.json\\ninternal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json\\ninternal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json\\ninternal/catalog/catalog_test.go\\ninternal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json\\ninternal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json\\ninternal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\\ninternal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json\\n====\\n<code>ax rpc serve --stdio --host-channel 1.0.0</code>, exclusively with\\nConfiguration 4.0.0 (Sections 6.6 and 11.10). The flag is accepted only on\\n<code>rpc serve --stdio</code>, exactly once with the literal value\\n<code>1.0.0</code>; a missing value, duplicate flag, other value or use on another\\ncommand is <code>invalid_arguments</code> (exit 2). The unflagged invocation\\nretains its legacy meaning. Both invocations are streaming exceptions to CLI\\nResult output: the new invocation emits only TLS records on stdout, including\\nencrypted RPC-5 frames after authentication, never a plaintext CLI result.\\n\\nThe v0.5.0 release adds exactly these TerminalBackend inspection commands:\\n\\n~~~text\\nax terminal backends list\\nax terminal backends show BACKEND_ID\\nax terminal backends probe BACKEND_ID\\nax terminal backends doctor [BACKEND_ID]\\n~~~\\n\\nThey map respectively to CLI Result 4 command tags\\n<code>terminal.backend.list</code>, <code>terminal.backend.show</code>,\\n<code>terminal.backend.probe</code>, and\\n<code>terminal.backend.doctor</code>. They are read-only and obey Sections 6.5\\nand 14.6; none is an activation command.\\n\\nFor the umbrella form, <code>--to</code> is permitted only with\\n<code>takeover</code> or <code>fork</code>, and <code>--as</code> is required and\\npermitted only with <code>fork</code>. <code>--workspace-mode</code> is permitted\\nonly with takeover and follows the cohort rule below. In non-interactive mode, takeover and\\nfork MUST include <code>--to</code>; <code>local</code> is the explicit local-host\\ntoken. Interactive takeover/fork MAY default <code>--to</code> to local only\\nafter displaying the resolved destination. <code>attach</code> always targets\\nthe resolved owner and accepts neither action-specific flag.\\n\\nThe umbrella form auto-executes only one uniquely safe non-mutating route.\\nEvery takeover, fork, move, or ambiguous result is displayed or serialized as\\na pure plan with its ownership/runtime effects and required confirmation. It\\nMUST NOT mutate while presenting the choice. Structured non-interactive mode\\nreturns <code>interactive_choice_required</code> when the exact action was not\\nselected.\\n\\n<code>--launch-plan FILE|-</code> names a file holding a Launch Plan request\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3534,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 884,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
